Because the length scales by the same factor as the coordinates. So if \([3,4]\) has length \(5\), then \(\left[\frac35,\frac45\right]\) has length:

\[
\sqrt{\left(\frac35\right)^2+\left(\frac45\right)^2}
=\sqrt{\frac{9}{25}+\frac{16}{25}}
=\sqrt{\frac{25}{25}}
=1
\]

So dividing each coordinate by 5 makes the whole vector’s length 1.
